---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii1_134",
  "series": "Band II 1 (1663 - 1685)",
  "seq": 134,
  "text": "<p> [[383.16]] <b>119. LEIBNIZ AN THOMAS HOBBES</p>\n<p> [[383.17]] [Paris, 1674.] [25.]</b></p>\n<p> [[384.7]] Illustri Viro Thomae Hobbesio </p>\n<p> [[384.8]] Gottfredus Guilielmus Leibnitius. </p>\n<p> [[384.9]] Non tam miraberis credo, Vir Clarissime, compellari Te ab ignoto, suetus ad omnia\n[[384.10]] humanitatis officia; quam a me, id est quando nulla alia re Tibi cognitus sum, ab harum\n[[384.11]] literarum autore quas non diffiteor rudes, neque Te dignas: addo et festinatas, quod non negabit\n[[384.12]] lator earum, vir optimus, qui eodem mecum hospitio Parisiis aliquandiu usus, pridie abitus sui\n[[384.13]] inter coenandum rogavit haberemne aliquid perferendum ad Te, nam aliquoties jam ante Tuum\n[[384.14]] nomen inter nos frequentatum erat, multo cum honore, quem virtutibus Tuis deberi constat. Ego\n[[384.15]] eo velut ictu excitatus, cum ille praesertim professus esset, notitiam Tecum jam a multo\n[[384.16]] tempore contractam, impetum scribendi de improviso sumsi, de quo prout videbitur statues,\n[[384.17]] nam si notitiam meam rejicis, non vitabis cultum. </p>\n<p> [[384.18]] Equidem diu est quod scripta tua versavi, digna seculo, digna Te, qui primus illam\n[[384.19]] accuratam disputandi ac demonstrandi rationem, veteribus velut per transennam inspectam, in\n[[384.20]] civilis scientiae clara luce posuisti: sed in libello <i>de Cive</i> Teipsum superasse videris, iis\n[[384.21]] rationum nervis, eo sententiarum pondere, ut saepe oracula potius reddere, quam dogmata\n[[384.22]] tradere credi possis. Ego, quem neque paradoxa deterrent, neque novitatis illecebrae abripiunt,\n[[384.23]] credidi operae pretium me facturum, si ipsas fibras interiores doctrinae tuae radicitus scrutarer:\n[[384.24]] neque enim ad conclusiones resistere meum est, neglectis demonstrationibus, quibus ab autore\n[[384.25]] muniuntur. </p>\n<p> [[384.26]] Principio igitur a naturae humanae contemplatione orsus, illud observas non hominibus\n[[384.27]] minus quam bestiis impetum quendam esse in obvia quaeque appetita involandi: hanc <b>spem</b>\n[[384.28]] solo <b>metu</b> frenari, quem facere possunt tot aliorum concurrentes in idem vires. Nam cum illud\n[[384.29]] posuisses id cuique jus esse, quod necessarium factu videatur ad incolumitatem tutandam, et\n[[384.30]] unumquemque necessitatum suarum judicem statuisses, facile conclusisti, justum omnibus in\n[[385.1]] omnes bellum eo rerum statu consecuturum. Quod cum internecinum esset futurum, ea virium\n[[385.2]] paritate, ut fortissimus a debilissimo occidi possit, inde pacis consilia agitari coepta. Hactenus\n[[385.3]] nihil habeo quod resistam: neque enim illud objiciam ferendas potius hujus vitae injurias, quam\n[[385.4]] periculo futurae repellendas; quaeque alia Theologi ac Jurisconsulti in Te congessere: satis\n[[385.5]] enim video demonstrationes tuas esse, ut in Geometria, universales et a materia abstractas;\n[[385.6]] quare etsi cuique jus tribuas faciendi quidvis tuendi sui causa, non negas, si quis sit Omnipotens,\n[[385.7]] si qua futura vita praemiis poenisque destinata, non tam veritatem theorematum desiisse,\n[[385.8]] quam applicationem cessare; incolumitatem enim cujusque his positis in vitae melioris\n[[385.9]] expectatione sitam et justum fore, quicquid cuique ad eam obtinendam utile videatur: denique\n[[385.10]] neque hujus vitae defensionem jure divino denegatam, etsi desinat in ea consistere summa\n[[385.11]] rerum. </p>\n<p> [[385.12]] Illud ergo nunc quaerendum est, qua ratione pax inita firmetur, nam si nulla est pacis\n[[385.13]] securitas, restat status belli, et jus cuilibet adversarium occupandi. In eum ergo usum Respublicas\n[[385.14]] ais inventas, quae mutuo complurium consensu armatae, tutos omnes praestare possint.\n[[385.15]] Etsi autem videaris asserere, jus omne a subditis in Rempublicam translatum; recte tamen alibi\n[[385.16]] agnoscis, etiam in Republica jus restare consulendi rebus suis, ubi perniciei metus sive in\n[[385.17]] Republica, sive ab ipsa Republica immineat: quare si quis jussu eorum penes quos rerum\n[[385.18]] summa est ad supplicium trahatur, jus ipsi utique esse, miscendi ima summis, salutis causa; sed\n[[385.19]] caeteros ex vi primi pacti quietem rectoribus debere. Sed quaeso Te Vir Clarissime, nonne\n[[385.20]] fateberis non minus in Republica, quam in statu illo rudi, quem naturalem vocas, suspicionem\n[[385.21]] validam periculi ingentis justam esse praeveniendi mali causam. Quodsi ergo manifeste appareat\n[[385.22]] innocentes plecti, si saepe si indiscriminatim saeviat tyrannis; non diffiteberis opinor, jus\n[[385.23]] esse ex tuae quoque philosophiae decretis, coeundi in foedera illis qui periculo propinqui\n[[385.24]] videntur. Nam illud Tibi facile assentior, plebem promiscuam, rectius facturam, dum vivere\n[[385.25]] commode liceat, si indignationi suae, aut miserationi, aliisque animi motibus extra metum\n[[386.1]] [non] posthabeat quietem suam. Quare summa eorum omnium quae de summa potestate tute\n[[386.2]] concludis, huc redire videtur: in Republica, neque tam facile neque ob suspiciones tam leves\n[[386.3]] abrumpendum foedus, quoniam major in ea securitas praestetur. At major longe Christianorum\n[[386.4]] veterum patientia fuit, qui quandam ut ita dicam irresistibilitatem tribuebant Reipublicae. </p>\n",
  "number": "119.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ AN THOMAS HOBBES",
  "date": "[Paris, 1674.] [25.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:119. LEIBNIZ AN THOMAS HOBBES [Paris, 1674.] [25.] Illustri Viro Thomae Hobbesio Gottfredus Guilielmus Leibnitius. Non tam miraberis credo, Vir Clarissime, compellari Te ab ignoto, suetus ad omnia humanitatis officia; quam a me, id est quando nulla alia re Tibi cognitus sum, ab harum literarum autor...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>